l names into bash_exec commands.\n- Keep stdout concise; if persistent command logs are needed, use pipeline logging to project files (e.g., `cmd 2>&1 | tee reports/<task_desc>/run.log`) and print short summaries.\n- Always provide file or directory paths as relative paths; they will be resolved relative to the project files root.\n", "additional_kwargs": {}, "response_metadata": {}, "type": "system", "name": null, "id": null, "__class__": "SystemMessage", "__type__": "system"}
12:16:35 INFO catmaster.runtime.artifact_callback | [llm.context.message] model=openai/gpt-5.3-codex:online callback_run_id=019cacc3-2197-77e1-9185-2c71f7c84e28 batch=0 idx=1 class=HumanMessage type=human payload={"content": "<context_pack>\nTask goal:\nGenerate a gas-phase O₂ structure in a large cubic box and write it as a VASP POSCAR (.vasp) plus optional .xyz.\n\nTask detail:\nUse RDKit-based tool `create_molecule_from_smiles` with SMILES `O=O` to build a 3D O2 molecule, then place it in a cubic cell with ~20 Å lattice (≈10 Å padding to images) and write to `structures/o2/o2.vasp` (and `structures/o2/o2.xyz` if supported). Ensure the two atoms are the only atoms, species order is O O, and initial bond length is reasonable (~1.2 Å). After writing, verify by quick parse (e.g., via a short python snippet) that: (1) lattice vectors correspond to ~20 Å cube, (2) Cartesian distance between O atoms is ~1.1–1.3 Å, (3) molecule is not near a boundary (centered within a few Å).\n\nExpected outputs:\n- structures/o2/o2.vasp exists and contains a 20 Å-ish cubic lattice with 2 oxygen atoms\n- (Optional) structures/o2/o2.xyz exists\n- A short stdout summary reporting cell lengths and initial O–O distance\n\nSuggested tools:\ncreate_molecule_from_smiles, bash_exec\n\nReference hint:\n- If create_molecule_from_smiles does not natively support setting the box, generate coordinates then use a small python/ASE script to wrap into a 20 Å cube and write .vasp/.xyz.\n- Prefer Cartesian coordinates for distance check; for VASP POSCAR, either Direct or Cartesian is fine.\n\nWorkspace policy:\nProject files policy:\n- Current files root: /home/chenhh/python_projects/CatMaster/project_space/test_o2_9/files\n- Tool path params are resolved relative to this files root.\n- Metadata is internal; do not read or write metadata paths from tasks.\n- Use progressive disclosure: locate with rg, then read small excerpts with sed/head/tail.\n- Do not cat large files into context. Persist large outputs and cite paths.\n- Role: task_runner\n\nMemory index excerpt:\n# MEMORY (AUTOLOADED INDEX)\n\n## What this is\n- Autoloaded memory index for this project.\n- Keep this file concise and pointer-first.\n- Put details in MEMORY/topics/*.md.\n\n## Latest State\n- Current focus: Compute O2 in a box: prepare VASP inputs from scratch, DO perform VASP calculation to get the results, and report final energy per atom and O–O bond distance from vasp results.\n- Current milestone: Execution plan approved and committed (task_id=plan_commit, 2026-03-02).\n- Latest run artifact: No file artifact from planning run; plan details captured in MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2).\n- Next action: WP1 — generate gas-phase O2 structure in a sufficiently large cubic box (POSCAR/XYZ).\n\n## Top Constraints\n1. (empty)\n\n## Active Open Questions\n1. (empty)\n\n## Pointers\n- Facts / decisions: MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md\n- Files / artifacts: MEMORY/topics/FILES.md\n- Constraints: MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md\n- Open questions: MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md\n- Runbook: MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md\n\n## Keyword Map\n- GOAL: objective, success criteria, scope, non-goals\n- FACTS: definition, verified, result, decision\n- FILES: path, artifact, dataset, output, script\n- CONSTRAINTS: must, cannot, policy, budget\n- QUESTIONS: unknown, blocked, clarify, decide\n- RUNBOOK: steps, checklist, verify\n\n</context_pack>\n", "additional_kwargs": {}, "response_metadata": {}, "type": "human", "name": null, "id": "63c68c73-fc7f-4c0f-a29f-96a2d0e494f2", "__class__": "HumanMessage", "__type__": "human"}
