12:18:25 INFO catmaster.agents.graph | [graph.stream.messages] node=run_task field=runner_messages idx=0 payload={"content": "<context_pack>\nTask goal:\nPrepare VASP relaxation inputs for gas-phase O₂ with triplet spin enforcement.\n\nTask detail:\nUse vasp_relax_prepare on structures/o2/o2.vasp with calc_type='gas' and output_dir='vasp_inputs/o2_relax'. Ensure Γ-only KPOINTS (1×1×1) and gas preset settings (ISYM=0, LREAL=False, ISIF=2). Override INCAR via user_incar_settings to enforce triplet: ISPIN=2, NUPDOWN=2, MAGMOM set for two O atoms (e.g., '1 1' or '2*1'). Keep tight MP defaults (EDIFF=1e-6, EDIFFG=-0.02, NSW~500). After generation, validate that INCAR/KPOINTS/POSCAR/POTCAR exist and that INCAR contains NUPDOWN and MAGMOM; report any POTCAR-generation issues explicitly.\n\nExpected outputs:\n- Directory vasp_inputs/o2_relax/ containing INCAR, KPOINTS, POSCAR, POTCAR\n- A brief validation readout (grep) showing INCAR has ISPIN=2, NUPDOWN=2, MAGMOM=... and gas preset flags (ISYM=0, LREAL=F)\n- If tool errors (e.g., POTCAR not found), the exact error message and what files (if any) were written\n\nSuggested tools:\nvasp_relax_prepare, bash_exec\n\nReference hint:\n- Input structure: structures/o2/o2.vasp (already verified cubic ~21.15 Å, O–O ~1.151 Å)\n- Target output: vasp_inputs/o2_relax/\n\nWorkspace policy:\nProject files policy:\n- Current files root: /home/chenhh/python_projects/CatMaster/project_space/test_o2_9/files\n- Tool path params are resolved relative to this files root.\n- Metadata is internal; do not read or write metadata paths from tasks.\n- Use progressive disclosure: locate with rg, then read small excerpts with sed/head/tail.\n- Do not cat large files into context. Persist large outputs and cite paths.\n- Role: task_runner\n\nMemory index excerpt:\n# MEMORY (AUTOLOADED INDEX)\n\n## What this is\n- Autoloaded memory index for this project.\n- Keep this file concise and pointer-first.\n- Put details in MEMORY/topics/*.md.\n\n## Latest State\n- Current focus: Compute O2 in a box: prepare VASP inputs from scratch, DO perform VASP calculation to get the results, and report final energy per atom and O–O bond distance from vasp results.\n- Current milestone: WP1 completed (task_id=task_01, 2026-03-02): generated gas-phase O2 structure files and verified geometry/cell invariants.\n- Latest run artifact: structures/o2/o2.vasp and structures/o2/o2.xyz created; verification details captured in MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md and inventory in MEMORY/topics/FILES.md.\n- Next action: WP2 — prepare VASP relaxation inputs with triplet-spin enforcement.\n\n## Top Constraints\n1. (empty)\n\n## Active Open Questions\n1. (empty)\n\n## Pointers\n- Facts / decisions: MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md\n- Files / artifacts: MEMORY/topics/FILES.md\n- Constraints: MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md\n- Open questions: MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md\n- Runbook: MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md\n\n## Keyword Map\n- GOAL: objective, success criteria, scope, non-goals\n- FACTS: definition, verified, result, decision\n- FILES: path, artifact, dataset, output, script\n- CONSTRAINTS: must, cannot, policy, budget\n- QUESTIONS: unknown, blocked, clarify, decide\n- RUNBOOK: steps, checklist, verify\n\n</context_pack>\n", "additional_kwargs": {}, "response_metadata": {}, "type": "human", "name": null, "id": "422799bd-1632-402e-a431-c40a54a70dd8"}
