l names into bash_exec commands.\n- Keep stdout concise; if persistent command logs are needed, use pipeline logging to project files (e.g., `cmd 2>&1 | tee reports/<task_desc>/run.log`) and print short summaries.\n- Always provide file or directory paths as relative paths; they will be resolved relative to the project files root.\n", "additional_kwargs": {}, "response_metadata": {}, "type": "system", "name": null, "id": null, "__class__": "SystemMessage", "__type__": "system"}
12:26:14 INFO catmaster.runtime.artifact_callback | [llm.context.message] model=openai/gpt-5.3-codex:online callback_run_id=019caccb-f9ef-71f0-b24f-e8096defd086 batch=0 idx=1 class=HumanMessage type=human payload={"content": "<context_pack>\nTask goal:\nPrepare and run a VASP single-point (NSW=0) calculation for O2 using the relaxed geometry from the completed relaxation run.\n\nTask detail:\n1) Locate the relaxed structure file from the relaxation outputs (prefer CONTCAR in the relax run output directory). 2) Run vasp_sp_prepare with calc_type='gas' (Gamma-only) to generate SP inputs under vasp_inputs/o2_sp/o2 (or analogous). 3) Ensure triplet is enforced in the SP INCAR: ISPIN=2, NUPDOWN=2, and a sensible MAGMOM (e.g., 1 1) if not already present; patch INCAR if the prepare tool doesn’t pass user_incar_settings. 4) Execute VASP in single-folder mode for that SP input directory, writing outputs under vasp_runs/o2_sp/.... 5) Validate normal termination and that key output files exist (OUTCAR, OSZICAR, vasprun.xml, and at least one of CONTCAR/POSCAR).\n\nExpected outputs:\n- Workspace-relative path to the SP input directory created by vasp_sp_prepare\n- Workspace-relative path to the SP output directory produced by vasp_execute_batch\n- One-line confirmation that OUTCAR shows normal termination (or equivalent)\n- File list check confirming presence of vasprun.xml and OUTCAR in the SP output directory\n\nSuggested tools:\nvasp_sp_prepare, vasp_execute_batch, bash_exec\n\nReference hint:\n- Relax outputs were previously written under vasp_runs/o2_relax/...; use its CONTCAR as the SP structure input.\n- If INCAR triplet keys are missing after vasp_sp_prepare, edit INCAR to add NUPDOWN=2 and MAGMOM=1 1 (or element-based equivalent).\n\nWorkspace policy:\nProject files policy:\n- Current files root: /home/chenhh/python_projects/CatMaster/project_space/test_o2_9/files\n- Tool path params are resolved relative to this files root.\n- Metadata is internal; do not read or write metadata paths from tasks.\n- Use progressive disclosure: locate with rg, then read small excerpts with sed/head/tail.\n- Do not cat large files into context. Persist large outputs and cite paths.\n- Role: task_runner\n\nMemory index excerpt:\n# MEMORY (AUTOLOADED INDEX)\n\n## What this is\n- Autoloaded memory index for this project.\n- Keep this file concise and pointer-first.\n- Put details in MEMORY/topics/*.md.\n\n## Latest State\n- Current focus: Compute O2 in a box: prepare VASP inputs from scratch, DO perform VASP calculation to get the results, and report final energy per atom and O–O bond distance from vasp results.\n- Current milestone: WP3 completed (task_id=task_03, 2026-03-02): gas-phase O2 triplet relaxation executed, finished normally, and met ionic/electronic convergence checks.\n- Latest run artifact: `vasp_runs/o2_relax/o2/o2` contains converged run outputs (`OUTCAR`, `OSZICAR`, `CONTCAR`, `vasprun.xml`); verification details are in `MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md`.\n- Next action: WP4 — extract/report final energy per atom and relaxed O–O bond distance from converged outputs.\n\n## Top Constraints\n1. (empty)\n\n## Active Open Questions\n1. (empty)\n\n## Pointers\n- Facts / decisions: MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md\n- Files / artifacts: MEMORY/topics/FILES.md\n- Constraints: MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md\n- Open questions: MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md\n- Runbook: MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md\n\n## Keyword Map\n- GOAL: objective, success criteria, scope, non-goals\n- FACTS: definition, verified, result, decision\n- FILES: path, artifact, dataset, output, script\n- CONSTRAINTS: must, cannot, policy, budget\n- QUESTIONS: unknown, blocked, clarify, decide\n- RUNBOOK: steps, checklist, verify\n\n</context_pack>\n", "additional_kwargs": {}, "response_metadata": {}, "type": "human", "name": null, "id": "ad0317b8-5f61-4c7e-ab21-c24816324e36", "__class__": "HumanMessage", "__type__": "human"}
