l names into bash_exec commands.\n- Keep stdout concise; if persistent command logs are needed, use pipeline logging to project files (e.g., `cmd 2>&1 | tee reports/<task_desc>/run.log`) and print short summaries.\n- Always provide file or directory paths as relative paths; they will be resolved relative to the project files root.\n", "additional_kwargs": {}, "response_metadata": {}, "type": "system", "name": null, "id": null, "__class__": "SystemMessage", "__type__": "system"}
12:29:26 INFO catmaster.runtime.artifact_callback | [llm.context.message] model=openai/gpt-5.3-codex:online callback_run_id=019cacce-e57f-7280-8db8-3f9800069da0 batch=0 idx=1 class=HumanMessage type=human payload={"content": "<context_pack>\nTask goal:\nExtract final total energy (and eV/atom) and O–O bond distance from the completed O2 VASP single-point run outputs.\n\nTask detail:\nUse the converged single-point directory `vasp_runs/o2_sp/CONTCAR` as source of truth. Parse final electronic total energy (TOTEN) from `OUTCAR` (last occurrence) or from `vasprun.xml` if available; report E_total (eV) and E_per_atom = E_total/2. Read final geometry from `CONTCAR` in the same SP run directory (or `POSCAR` if CONTCAR missing) and compute the O–O distance in Å from Cartesian positions (minimum-image not needed due to large box). Also perform a minimal sanity check: confirm 2 atoms and species are O,O; optionally confirm normal termination marker exists in OUTCAR. Write a machine-readable summary file under `results/` (e.g., `results/o2_vasp_summary.json`) containing: source_dir, energy_total_eV, energy_per_atom_eV, oo_distance_A, and timestamp. Keep scripts short and reproducible (bash_exec with a small Python snippet using ASE/pymatgen, with a simple regex fallback for TOTEN if needed).\n\nExpected outputs:\n- Printed values: total energy (eV), energy per atom (eV/atom), O–O bond length (Å), and the exact source file paths used.\n- A new results artifact saved under `results/` (JSON) with the extracted numbers and metadata.\n- A short note on any parsing fallbacks used (e.g., OUTCAR regex vs vasprun.xml).\n\nSuggested tools:\nbash_exec\n\nReference hint:\n- OUTCAR: search for last line containing 'free  energy   TOTEN  =' to get final energy.\n- Geometry: ASE can read VASP CONTCAR directly; then compute distance between the two atomic positions.\n- If vasprun.xml is present, pymatgen Vasprun can provide final_energy directly; otherwise parse OUTCAR.\n\nWorkspace policy:\nProject files policy:\n- Current files root: /home/chenhh/python_projects/CatMaster/project_space/test_o2_9/files\n- Tool path params are resolved relative to this files root.\n- Metadata is internal; do not read or write metadata paths from tasks.\n- Use progressive disclosure: locate with rg, then read small excerpts with sed/head/tail.\n- Do not cat large files into context. Persist large outputs and cite paths.\n- Role: task_runner\n\nMemory index excerpt:\n# MEMORY (AUTOLOADED INDEX)\n\n## What this is\n- Autoloaded memory index for this project.\n- Keep this file concise and pointer-first.\n- Put details in MEMORY/topics/*.md.\n\n## Latest State\n- Current focus: Compute O2 in a box: prepare VASP inputs from scratch, DO perform VASP calculation to get the results, and report final energy per atom and O–O bond distance from vasp results.\n- Current milestone: WP4 completed (task_id=task_04, 2026-03-02): O2 gas-phase single-point run from relaxed geometry executed with explicit triplet settings and normal termination verification.\n- Latest run artifacts: `vasp_inputs/o2_sp/CONTCAR` (prepared SP inputs) and `vasp_runs/o2_sp/CONTCAR` (completed SP outputs with `OUTCAR`, `OSZICAR`, `vasprun.xml`).\n- Next action: WP5 — extract/report final energy per atom and relaxed O–O bond distance from converged outputs.\n\n## Top Constraints\n1. (empty)\n\n## Active Open Questions\n1. (empty)\n\n## Pointers\n- Facts / decisions: MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md\n- Files / artifacts: MEMORY/topics/FILES.md\n- Constraints: MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md\n- Open questions: MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md\n- Runbook: MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md\n\n## Keyword Map\n- GOAL: objective, success criteria, scope, non-goals\n- FACTS: definition, verified, result, decision\n- FILES: path, artifact, dataset, output, script\n- CONSTRAINTS: must, cannot, policy, budget\n- QUESTIONS: unknown, blocked, clarify, decide\n- RUNBOOK: steps, checklist, verify\n\n</context_pack>\n", "additional_kwargs": {}, "response_