12:29:51 INFO catmaster.agents.graph | [graph.stream.messages] node=run_task field=runner_messages idx=0 payload={"content": "<context_pack>\nTask goal:\nExtract final total energy (and eV/atom) and O–O bond distance from the completed O2 VASP single-point run outputs.\n\nTask detail:\nUse the converged single-point directory `vasp_runs/o2_sp/CONTCAR` as source of truth. Parse final electronic total energy (TOTEN) from `OUTCAR` (last occurrence) or from `vasprun.xml` if available; report E_total (eV) and E_per_atom = E_total/2. Read final geometry from `CONTCAR` in the same SP run directory (or `POSCAR` if CONTCAR missing) and compute the O–O distance in Å from Cartesian positions (minimum-image not needed due to large box). Also perform a minimal sanity check: confirm 2 atoms and species are O,O; optionally confirm normal termination marker exists in OUTCAR. Write a machine-readable summary file under `results/` (e.g., `results/o2_vasp_summary.json`) containing: source_dir, energy_total_eV, energy_per_atom_eV, oo_distance_A, and timestamp. Keep scripts short and reproducible (bash_exec with a small Python snippet using ASE/pymatgen, with a simple regex fallback for TOTEN if needed).\n\nExpected outputs:\n- Printed values: total energy (eV), energy per atom (eV/atom), O–O bond length (Å), and the exact source file paths used.\n- A new results artifact saved under `results/` (JSON) with the extracted numbers and metadata.\n- A short note on any parsing fallbacks used (e.g., OUTCAR regex vs vasprun.xml).\n\nSuggested tools:\nbash_exec\n\nReference hint:\n- OUTCAR: search for last line containing 'free  energy   TOTEN  =' to get final energy.\n- Geometry: ASE can read VASP CONTCAR directly; then compute distance between the two atomic positions.\n- If vasprun.xml is present, pymatgen Vasprun can provide final_energy directly; otherwise parse OUTCAR.\n\nWorkspace policy:\nProject files policy:\n- Current files root: /home/chenhh/python_projects/CatMaster/project_space/test_o2_9/files\n- Tool path params are resolved relative to this files root.\n- Metadata is internal; do not read or write metadata paths from tasks.\n- Use progressive disclosure: locate with rg, then read small excerpts with sed/head/tail.\n- Do not cat large files into context. Persist large outputs and cite paths.\n- Role: task_runner\n\nMemory index excerpt:\n# MEMORY (AUTOLOADED INDEX)\n\n## What this is\n- Autoloaded memory index for this project.\n- Keep this file concise and pointer-first.\n- Put details in MEMORY/topics/*.md.\n\n## Latest State\n- Current focus: Compute O2 in a box: prepare VASP inputs from scratch, DO perform VASP calculation to get the results, and report final energy per atom and O–O bond distance from vasp results.\n- Current milestone: WP4 completed (task_id=task_04, 2026-03-02): O2 gas-phase single-point run from relaxed geometry executed with explicit triplet settings and normal termination verification.\n- Latest run artifacts: `vasp_inputs/o2_sp/CONTCAR` (prepared SP inputs) and `vasp_runs/o2_sp/CONTCAR` (completed SP outputs with `OUTCAR`, `OSZICAR`, `vasprun.xml`).\n- Next action: WP5 — extract/report final energy per atom and relaxed O–O bond distance from converged outputs.\n\n## Top Constraints\n1. (empty)\n\n## Active Open Questions\n1. (empty)\n\n## Pointers\n- Facts / decisions: MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md\n- Files / artifacts: MEMORY/topics/FILES.md\n- Constraints: MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md\n- Open questions: MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md\n- Runbook: MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md\n\n## Keyword Map\n- GOAL: objective, success criteria, scope, non-goals\n- FACTS: definition, verified, result, decision\n- FILES: path, artifact, dataset, output, script\n- CONSTRAINTS: must, cannot, policy, budget\n- QUESTIONS: unknown, blocked, clarify, decide\n- RUNBOOK: steps, checklist, verify\n\n</context_pack>\n", "additional_kwargs": {}, "response_metadata": {}, "type": "human", "name": null, "id": "e1ea3632-5b2b-4c6f-a01f-17aaaabad247"}
12:29:51 INFO catmaster.agents.graph | [graph.stream.messages] node=run_task field=runner_messages idx=1 payload={"content": "", "additional_kwargs": {"refusal": null}, "response_metadata": {"token_usage": {"completion_tokens": 1248, "prompt_tokens": 10357, "total_tokens": 11605, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": null, "reasoning_tokens": 222, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null, "image_tokens": 0}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 9216}, "cost": 0.02108155, "is_byok": false, "cost_details": {"upstream_inference_cost": 0.02108155, "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.00360955, "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 0.017472}}, "model_provider": "openai", "model_name": "openai/gpt-5.3-codex", "system_fingerprint": null, "id": "gen-1772425778-9WJxaX69j6ZzQrGQpwns", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "logprobs": null}, "type": "ai", "name": null, "id": "lc_run--019cacce-e57f-7280-8db8-3f9800069da0-0", "tool_calls": [{"name": "bash_exec", "args": {"script": "python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json, re\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n\nsource_dir = Path('vasp_runs/o2_sp/CONTCAR')\nif not source_dir.exists():\n    raise SystemExit(f\"Source dir not found: {source_dir}\")\n\noutcar = source_dir / 'OUTCAR'\nvasprun = source_dir / 'vasprun.xml'\ncontcar = source_dir / 'CONTCAR'\nposcar = source_dir / 'POSCAR'\ngeom_file = contcar if contcar.exists() else poscar\nif not geom_file.exists():\n    raise SystemExit(f\"Neither CONTCAR nor POSCAR found in {source_dir}\")\n\n# Geometry + sanity check with ASE\nfrom ase.io import read\natoms = read(str(geom_file))\nsyms = atoms.get_chemical_symbols()\nif len(syms) != 2:\n    raise SystemExit(f\"Sanity check failed: expected 2 atoms, got {len(syms)}\")\nif sorted(syms) != ['O', 'O']:\n    raise SystemExit(f\"Sanity check failed: expected O,O species, got {syms}\")\n\nd = atoms.get_distance(0, 1, mic=False)\n\n# Energy parse with vasprun preferred, OUTCAR fallback\nenergy = None\nenergy_source = None\nfallback_note = None\n\nif vasprun.exists():\n    try:\n        from pymatgen.io.vasp.outputs import Vasprun\n        vr = Vasprun(str(vasprun), parse_dos=False, parse_eigen=False, parse_projected_eigen=False)\n        energy = float(vr.final_energy)\n        energy_source = str(vasprun)\n        fallback_note = 'Used pymatgen Vasprun.final_energy from vasprun.xml.'\n    except Exception as e:\n        fallback_note = f'vasprun.xml parse failed ({type(e).__name__}); used OUTCAR regex fallback.'\n\nif energy is None:\n    if not outcar.exists():\n        raise SystemExit('Could not parse energy: vasprun unavailable/failed and OUTCAR missing.')\n    txt = outcar.read_text(errors='ignore')\n    matches = re.findall(r\"free\\s+energy\\s+TOTEN\\s*=\\s*([-+]?\\d*\\.\\d+|[-+]?\\d+)\", txt)\n    if not matches:\n        raise SystemExit('No TOTEN matches found in OUTCAR.')\n    energy = float(matches[-1])\n    energy_source = str(outcar)\n    if fallback_note is None:\n        fallback_note = 'Used OUTCAR regex parse of last TOTEN line (vasprun.xml not used).'\n\n# Optional normal termination marker check\ntermination_ok = None\nif outcar.exists():\n    tail = outcar.read_text(errors='ignore')[-200000:]\n    termination_ok = ('General timing and accounting informations for this job' in tail)\n\nenergy_per_atom = energy / 2.0\n\nresult = {\n    'source_dir': str(source_dir),\n    'energy_total_eV': energy,\n    'energy_per_atom_eV': energy_per_atom,\n    'oo_distance_A': float(d),\n    'timestamp': datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n    'energy_source_file': energy_source,\n    'geometry_source_file': str(geom_file),\n    'outcar_normal_termination_marker': termination_ok,\n    'parse_note': fallback_note,\n}\n\nresults_dir = Path('results')\nresults_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\nout_json = results_dir / 'o2_vasp_summary.json'\nout_json.write_text(json.dumps(result, indent=2))\n\nprint(f\"E_tota