12:29:51 INFO catmaster.llm.factory | [llm.http.raw_post] provider=openrouter model=openai/gpt-5.3-codex:online method=POST url=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions body={"messages":[{"content":"\nYou are a memory patch editor for a materials computation agent.\n\nOutput contract:\n- Output ONLY Aider SEARCH/REPLACE edit blocks.\n- Do NOT output explanations.\n- Do NOT use markdown code fences.\n\nRequired edit format:\n<relative/path/to/file>\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n... exact existing text ...\n=======\n... replacement text ...\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n\nScope:\n- Allowed paths to modify: MEMORY/** only.\n- Never modify any other path.\n\nMemory rules:\n- Memory is a scientific interface, not an execution transcript.\n- Prefer reusable invariants:\n  1) System invariants (reference states, structure IDs, naming, units/definitions)\n  2) Method/protocol invariants (comparability-critical settings/definitions)\n  3) Result invariants (final reusable values with units/conditions/evidence path)\n- Do NOT copy raw logs/tool traces into MEMORY.\n- Do NOT add empty placeholder blocks (for constraints/questions/etc.).\n- Keep section schema stable so downstream parsers still work (e.g., Top Constraints / Active Open Questions headings).\n- Treat `MEMORY/MEMORY.md` as a latest-state snapshot; finalizer (`task_id == \"finalize_memory\"`) must write run-final state.\n- In `FACTS.md`, keep reusable scientific facts/method constraints/key conclusions with evidence; move path/layout tactics to `RUNBOOK.md`, and avoid pure path-layout Decision Log entries unless scientific interpretation changes.\n\nTopic schema contract:\n- `MEMORY/topics/GOAL.md`:\n  - Keep objective, definition of success, non-goals, and scope boundary.\n  - Do not put run-by-run logs or tool traces here.\n- `MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md`:\n  - For key results, include condition/method, units, and evidence path.\n- `MEMORY/topics/FILES.md`:\n  - Keep reusable file/artifact index records.\n  - Prefer normalized records: `- PATH: <rel_path> | kind=<kind> | desc=<desc> | source=<task_id>`.\n- `MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md`:\n  - Keep hard constraints and soft preferences, with short source context when possible.\n- `MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md`:\n  - Keep unresolved blockers in Active and move resolved items to Resolved with closure evidence.\n- `MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md`:\n  - Keep stable reusable operating checklist and common recovery playbook.\n- `MEMORY/MEMORY.md`:\n  - Keep pointer-first index and concise state only.\n  - Do not duplicate detailed facts/path inventories from topic files.\n\nAdditional caution:\n- Text matching rules:\n  - Treat only text inside `<editable_file path=\"...\">...</editable_file>` as existing file content.\n  - If adding new content, anchor under an existing heading from the editable file text.\n- File-role routing:\n  - Keep `MEMORY/MEMORY.md` concise and pointer-first (current state + short summaries + pointers).\n  - Put reusable facts/decisions into `MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md`.\n  - Put artifact/path index entries into `MEMORY/topics/FILES.md` (prefer `- PATH:` records).\n  - Keep constraints/questions/runbook updates in their corresponding topic files.\n- Write-routing from task structured result:\n  - `facts` and `decisions` -> `MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md`\n  - `files` and `artifacts` -> `MEMORY/topics/FILES.md`\n  - `constraints` -> `MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md`\n  - `open_questions` -> `MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md`\n  - goal/success-boundary changes -> `MEMORY/topics/GOAL.md`\n  - reusable procedure/checklist updates -> `MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md`\n- Minimality gate:\n  - Update only when content adds durable scientific value (system/method/result invariants, reusable decisions, stable constraints).\n  - Do NOT materialize every structured_result field by default.\n  - Skip low-value procedural chatter, repeated confirmations, or transient execution narration.\n  - `open_questions` should contain unresolved blockers only; drop speculative/self-referential questions.\n- Merge-first policy for `MEMORY/topics/FILES.md`:\n  - Do NOT append blindly. Canonicalize and merge before writing.\n  - Treat `PATH` as the merge key (workspace-relative, normalized form).\n  - If a `PATH` entry already exists, update that record (kind/desc/source) instead of adding a duplicate line.\n  - Keep at most 1 canonical record per `PATH`.\n  - Keep `source` concise and deduplicated (prefer latest run/task context; avoid long source history).\n  - Exclude routine internal audit logs (`metadata/**`, `audit/**`, `.logs/**`) unless they are uniquely required evidence.\n  - Include scripts only when they are primary/reusable scripts referenced by summary/facts.\n  - Exclude intermediate scratch files and one-off patch helpers unless they are required for scientific reproducibility.\n  - Prefer scientific reusable artifacts over run-noise.\n- Conflict precedence:\n  - If `MEMORY/MEMORY.md` conflicts with `FACTS.md` or `FILES.md`, topic files are authoritative.\n  - Keep single-source updates; avoid duplicating the same fact/path across multiple files.\n- Quality checks before output:\n  - Ensure detailed facts and path inventories are not dumped into `MEMORY/MEMORY.md`.\n  - Ensure key claims include evidence path pointers.\n  - Ensure `FILES.md` path records follow the `- PATH:` style where applicable.\n  - Ensure `FILES.md` has no duplicate `PATH` records after merge.\n  - Ensure `QUESTIONS.md` reflects Active vs Resolved transitions when answers are available.\n","role":"system"},{"content":"\nRun id: run_20260302_041302_4e65c2\nTask id: task_05\nTask goal (short): Extract final total energy (and eV/atom) and O–O bond distance from the completed O2 VASP single-point run outputs.\nOutcome: success\n\nTask structured result (JSON):\n{\"summary\": \"Extracted final O2 single-point energy and bond length from `vasp_runs/o2_sp/CONTCAR` and wrote machine-readable summary to `results/o2_vasp_summary.json`. Energy was read from `vasprun.xml` (pymatgen), geometry from `CONTCAR` (ASE), with sanity checks (2 atoms, O/O) and OUTCAR normal-termination marker check.\", \"facts\": [\"Source directory used: `vasp_runs/o2_sp/CONTCAR`.\", \"Final total energy: -9.88463003 eV (from `vasp_runs/o2_sp/CONTCAR/vasprun.xml`).\", \"Energy per atom: -4.942315015 eV/atom.\", \"O–O bond distance: 1.233252560278 Å (from `vasp_runs/o2_sp/CONTCAR/CONTCAR`).\", \"Sanity checks passed: atom count = 2, species = O and O.\", \"OUTCAR normal termination marker present: True.\", \"Parsing fallback note: no fallback needed; used `Vasprun.final_energy` from `vasprun.xml`.\"], \"files\": [{\"path\": \"results/o2_vasp_summary.json\", \"description\": \"Machine-readable summary of source directory, energies, O–O distance, timestamp, and parse metadata.\", \"kind\": \"output\"}], \"constraints\": [], \"open_questions\": [], \"decisions\": [{\"decision\": \"Use `vasprun.xml` as primary energy source and only fallback to OUTCAR TOTEN regex if needed.\", \"rationale\": \"Task detail requested OUTCAR last TOTEN or vasprun.xml if available; vasprun.xml was available and parsed successfully.\"}], \"next_steps\": [], \"artifacts\": [\"results/o2_vasp_summary.json\"]}\n\nEditable file snapshot (authoritative):\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/MEMORY.md\">\n# MEMORY (AUTOLOADED INDEX)\n\n## What this is\n- Autoloaded memory index for this project.\n- Keep this file concise and pointer-first.\n- Put details in MEMORY/topics/*.md.\n\n## Latest State\n- Current focus: Compute O2 in a box: prepare VASP inputs from scratch, DO perform VASP calculation to get the results, and report final energy per atom and O–O bond distance from vasp results.\n- Current milestone: WP4 completed (task_id=task_04, 2026-03-02): O2 gas-phase single-point run from relaxed geometry executed with explicit triplet settings and normal termination verification.\n- Latest run artifacts: `vasp_inputs/o2_sp/CONTCAR` (prepared SP inputs) and `vasp_runs/o2_sp/CONTCAR` (completed SP outputs with `OUTCAR`, `OSZICAR`, `vasprun.xml`).\n- Next action: WP5 — extract/report final energy per atom and relaxed O–O bond distance from converged outputs.\n\n## Top Constraints\n1. (empty)\n\n## Active Open Questions\n1. (empty)\n\n## Pointers\n- Goal / principles: MEMORY/topics/GOAL.md\n- Facts / decisions: MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md\n- Files / artifacts: MEMORY/topics/FILES.md\n- Constraints: MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md\n- Open questions: MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md\n- Runbook: MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md\n\n## Keyword Map\n- GOAL: objective, success criteria, scope, non-goals\n- FACTS: definition, verified, result, decision\n- FILES: path, artifact, dataset, output, script\n- CONSTRAINTS: must, cannot, policy, budget\n- QUESTIONS: unknown, blocked, clarify, decide\n- RUNBOOK: steps, checklist, verify\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/GOAL.md\">\n# GOAL\n\n## TL;DR\n- Primary objective: Compute O2 in a box: prepare VASP inputs from scratch, DO perform VASP calculation to get the results, and report final energy per atom and O–O bond distance from vasp results.\n- Definition of success:\n- Non-goals:\n\n## Objectives\n- (empty)\n\n## Success Criteria\n- (empty)\n\n## Non-goals\n- (empty)\n\n## Change log\n- [2026-03-02] Compute O2 in a box: prepare VASP inputs from scratch, DO perform VASP calculation to get the results, and report final energy per atom and O–O bond distance from vasp results.\n\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/FACTS.md\">\n# FACTS\n\n## TL;DR\n- Canonical definitions: Gas-phase O2 reference setup uses triplet spin in a large cubic box with standard PBE/PAW settings.\n- Verified facts: Planning is committed, WP1 structure-generation invariants are satisfied, WP2 VASP relaxation inputs were generated with gas-phase controls and explicit triplet enforcement, WP3 relaxation run finished normally with convergence/triplet consistency, and WP4 single-point inputs/run from relaxed geometry completed with normal termination.\n- Tentative hypotheses: (empty)\n\n## Canonical Definitions\n- Gas-phase O2 project setup target (planning baseline): PBE (PAW_PBE 5.4 / MPRelaxSet), cubic box with ~10 Å padding (~20 Å cell), and triplet state (S=1) enforced via spin controls (e.g., NUPDOWN/MAGMOM).\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=plan_commit).\n\n## Verified Facts\n- Plan status: committed for execution.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.summary (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=plan_commit).\n\n- Approved execution decomposition: 5 work packages (WP1–WP5).\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts + structured_result.next_steps (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=plan_commit).\n\n- WP1 output generated: `structures/o2/o2.vasp` exists and contains 2 oxygen atoms.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts[0] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_01).\n\n- Companion geometry export exists: `structures/o2/o2.xyz`.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts[1] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_01).\n\n- Parsed POSCAR geometry invariants (ASE verification): cubic cell lengths = 21.151, 21.151, 21.151 Å.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts[2] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_01).\n\n- Parsed O–O Cartesian bond distance = 1.151 Å (within expected molecular range for initial O2 geometry).\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts[3] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_01).\n\n- Species order in parsed POSCAR is `O O`.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts[4] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_01).\n\n- Molecule is centered in the box: COM = (10.575, 10.575, 10.575) Å with minimum boundary clearance 10.575 Å.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts[5] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_01).\n\n- WP2 preparation succeeded: `vasp_relax_prepare` ran on `structures/o2/o2.vasp` with `calc_type=gas`, producing `vasp_inputs/o2_relax/o2`.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts[0] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_02).\n\n- Prepared VASP input set is complete at `vasp_inputs/o2_relax/o2`: `INCAR`, `KPOINTS`, `POSCAR`, `POTCAR` all present.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts[1] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_02).\n\n- INCAR gas-relaxation controls validated: `EDIFF=1e-06`, `EDIFFG=-0.02` (eV/Å force criterion), `NSW=500`, `ISIF=2`, `ISYM=0`, `LREAL=False`.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts[2] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_02).\n\n- Triplet-spin invariants are explicitly present in INCAR: `ISPIN=2`, `NUPDOWN=2`, `MAGMOM=2*1`.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts[3] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_02).\n\n- KPOINTS sampling is Γ-only `1×1×1`, consistent with isolated molecule in large box.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts[4] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_02).\n\n- WP3 execution succeeded via `vasp_execute_batch`; produced run directory `vasp_runs/o2_relax/o2/o2`.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts[0] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_03).\n\n- OUTCAR completion checks indicate normal termination; no common fatal-error signatures were detected.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts[1], structured_result.facts[2] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_03).\n\n- Ionic convergence satisfied: final max force = 0.005452 eV/Å, below `|EDIFFG| = 0.02` eV/Å (`EDIFFG=-0.02`); run did not terminate by `NSW` exhaustion.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts[3], structured_result.facts[4], structured_result.facts[5] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_03).\n\n- Final total free energy from OUTCAR: `TOTEN = -9.88462988 eV`.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts[6] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_03).\n\n- Final ionic step has electronic convergence in OSZICAR (`electronic_converged_final_ionic=true`).\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts[9] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_03).\n\n- Spin-state consistency at run end: `NUPDOWN=2.0`; final total magnetic moment = 1.9999996 μB (triplet-consistent for O2).\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts[7], structured_result.facts[8] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_03).\n\n- Relaxed structure used as single-point start geometry: `vasp_runs/o2_relax/o2/o2/CONTCAR`.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts[0] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_04).\n\n- WP4 preparation succeeded: `vasp_sp_prepare` with `calc_type=gas` produced `vasp_inputs/o2_sp/CONTCAR`.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts[1] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_04).\n\n- Triplet controls in single-point INCAR were verified as present: `ISPIN=2`, `MAGMOM=1 1`, `NUPDOWN=2`.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts[2] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_04).\n\n- WP4 execution succeeded via `vasp_execute_batch`; single-point output directory is `vasp_runs/o2_sp/CONTCAR`.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts[3] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_04).\n\n- OUTCAR completion check for single-point run indicates normal termination (`General timing and accounting informations for this job` present).\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts[4] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_04).\n\n- Required single-point outputs are present in `vasp_runs/o2_sp/CONTCAR`: `OUTCAR`, `OSZICAR`, `vasprun.xml`, and geometry file condition (`CONTCAR`/`POSCAR`) satisfied.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.facts[5] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_04).\n\n## Tentative\n- (empty)\n\n## Decision Log\n- [2026-03-02] Plan committed.\n  - Rationale: Approved for execution.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.decisions[0] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=plan_commit).\n\n- [2026-03-02] Kept RDKit-generated padded box as-is for WP1 structure artifact.\n  - Rationale: Geometry already satisfied comparability-critical invariants (~20 Å class cubic cell, centered molecule, reasonable O–O bond length).\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.decisions[0] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_01).\n\n- [2026-03-02] Patched INCAR after generation to add/override `NUPDOWN` and `MAGMOM` for explicit triplet enforcement.\n  - Rationale: Preparation tool schema did not expose direct `user_incar_settings`; minimal post-generation edit preserved required spin invariants.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.decisions[0] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_02).\n\n- [2026-03-02] No rerun/fix cycle applied after WP3 execution.\n  - Rationale: Initial run already passed normal-finish checks and convergence criteria (ionic force + final-step SCF) with triplet-consistent spin readback.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.decisions[0] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_03).\n\n- [2026-03-02] Used the relaxation `CONTCAR` directly as the single-point starting geometry.\n  - Rationale: Task explicitly prefers the relaxed geometry from the completed relaxation run.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.decisions[0] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_04).\n\n- [2026-03-02] Patched single-point INCAR post-generation to enforce `NUPDOWN=2` and `MAGMOM=1 1`.\n  - Rationale: Generated INCAR did not fully match required triplet controls; explicit enforcement preserves spin-state comparability.\n  - Evidence: task packet structured_result.decisions[1] (run_id=run_20260302_041302_4e65c2, task_id=task_04).\n\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/FILES.md\">\n# FILES\n\n## TL;DR\n- Entry points: structures/o2/o2.vasp, vasp_inputs/o2_relax/o2, vasp_inputs/o2_sp/CONTCAR, vasp_runs/o2_sp/CONTCAR\n- Primary artifacts: structures/o2/o2.vasp, vasp_runs/o2_relax/o2/o2/CONTCAR, vasp_inputs/o2_sp/CONTCAR/INCAR, vasp_runs/o2_sp/CONTCAR/OUTCAR\n\n## Index\n- PATH: structures/o2/o2.vasp | kind=output | desc=Gas-phase O2 in a large cubic VASP cell (2 O atoms; cubic cell ~21.151 Å) | source=task_01\n- PATH: structures/o2/o2.xyz | kind=output | desc=Gas-phase O2 XYZ coordinates matching the POSCAR geometry | source=task_01\n- PATH: vasp_inputs/o2_relax/o2 | kind=dir | desc=Prepared VASP relaxation input set for gas-phase O2 (INCAR/KPOINTS/POSCAR/POTCAR) with triplet enforcement applied in INCAR | source=task_02\n- PATH: vasp_inputs/o2_sp/CONTCAR | kind=dir | desc=Prepared VASP single-point input directory for O2 using relaxed CONTCAR geometry (gas-phase setup) | source=task_04\n- PATH: vasp_inputs/o2_sp/CONTCAR/INCAR | kind=output | desc=Single-point INCAR with explicit triplet controls (`ISPIN=2`, `NUPDOWN=2`, `MAGMOM=1 1`) | source=task_04\n- PATH: vasp_runs/o2_relax/o2/_BATCH_STATE.json | kind=output | desc=DPDispatcher batch execution state record for O2 relaxation run submission/execution | source=task_03\n- PATH: vasp_runs/o2_relax/o2/o2 | kind=dir | desc=Completed O2 gas-phase relaxation run directory containing VASP outputs | source=task_03\n- PATH: vasp_runs/o2_relax/o2/o2/CONTCAR | kind=output | desc=Relaxed final geometry from converged O2 run | source=task_03\n- PATH: vasp_runs/o2_relax/o2/o2/OSZICAR | kind=output | desc=Ionic/electronic iteration summary for converged O2 relaxation | source=task_03\n- PATH: vasp_runs/o2_relax/o2/o2/OUTCAR | kind=output | desc=Primary run log with termination, force, energy, and magnetization readback used for convergence verification | source=task_03\n- PATH: vasp_runs/o2_relax/o2/o2/vasprun.xml | kind=output | desc=Structured XML results for the converged O2 relaxation | source=task_03\n- PATH: vasp_runs/o2_sp/CONTCAR | kind=dir | desc=Completed O2 single-point run directory from relaxed geometry | source=task_04\n- PATH: vasp_runs/o2_sp/CONTCAR/OSZICAR | kind=output | desc=SCF iteration summary for O2 single-point calculation | source=task_04\n- PATH: vasp_runs/o2_sp/CONTCAR/OUTCAR | kind=output | desc=Primary log for O2 single-point run with normal-termination confirmation | source=task_04\n- PATH: vasp_runs/o2_sp/CONTCAR/vasprun.xml | kind=output | desc=Structured XML results for completed O2 single-point run | source=task_04\n\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/CONSTRAINTS.md\">\n# CONSTRAINTS\n\n## TL;DR\n- Hard constraints:\n  - (empty)\n\n## Hard Constraints\n- (empty)\n\n## Soft Preferences\n- (empty)\n\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/QUESTIONS.md\">\n# QUESTIONS\n\n## TL;DR\n- Active blockers: (empty)\n\n## Active\n- (empty)\n\n## Resolved\n- (empty)\n\n</editable_file>\n<editable_file path=\"MEMORY/topics/RUNBOOK.md\">\n# RUNBOOK\n\n## TL;DR\n- Standard operating procedure pointer file.\n- For gas-phase open-shell molecules (e.g., O2), include an explicit post-generation INCAR validation/patch step for spin invariants when generator schema is restrictive.\n- After execution, perform a compact completion/convergence check using OUTCAR + OSZICAR before deciding on rerun.\n\n## Checklist\n1. Confirm goal and success criteria from task packet.\n2. Read MEMORY.md first, then locate details via rg/sed.\n3. Persist large outputs to files and cite paths.\n4. For VASP gas-phase setup, verify comparability-critical controls (`ISYM=0`, `LREAL=False`, `ISIF=2`, Γ-only `1 1 1`).\n5. For triplet O2, verify `ISPIN=2`, `NUPDOWN=2`, and `MAGMOM=2*1`; if missing due to generator limitations, apply minimal INCAR post-edit and re-validate.\n6. After VASP execution, verify normal completion and convergence: OUTCAR normal termination + no fatal signatures, final max force below `|EDIFFG|`, and `nsw_exhausted=false`.\n7. Confirm final ionic-step electronic convergence from OSZICAR and spin readback consistency in OUTCAR (e.g., `NUPDOWN`, final total magnetic moment for triplet O2).\n8. Finish by returning one structured TaskOutput response.\n\n</editable_file>\n","role":"user"}],"model":"openai/gpt-5.3-codex:online","reasoning_effort":"high","stream":false,"temperature":1.0,"prompt_cache_retention":"24h"}
