k consistency in OUTCAR (e.g., `NUPDOWN`, final total magnetic moment for triplet O2).\n8. For final energy reporting, prefer `vasprun.xml` (`Vasprun.final_energy`) and only fallback to final OUTCAR `TOTEN` parsing if XML is unavailable.\n9. For molecular metrics, read final geometry from `CONTCAR`, verify expected species/atom count, and report O–O distance plus eV/atom consistently.\n10. Persist a machine-readable summary artifact and finish by returning one structured TaskOutput response.\n\n</editable_file>\n", "additional_kwargs": {}, "response_metadata": {}, "type": "human", "name": null, "id": null, "__class__": "HumanMessage", "__type__": "human"}
