d the O–O bond distance from the VASP results.\\n\\nKey numerical results (from VASP outputs)\\n- Final total energy (TOTEN): -9.88463003 eV\\n  - Source: vasp_runs/o2_sp/CONTCAR/vasprun.xml\\n- Energy per atom: -4.942315015 eV/atom\\n  - Source: derived from TOTEN for 2 atoms; see vasprun.xml\\n- O–O bond distance: 1.233252560278 Å\\n  - Source: vasp_runs/o2_sp/CONTCAR/CONTCAR\\n\\nConvergence and quality indicators\\n- OUTCAR indicates normal termination (no fatal errors).\\n- Final ionic max force: 0.005452 eV/Å\\n- Convergence criterion (EDIFFG): -0.02 eV/Å; achieved since final force (0.005452) < 0.02\\n- Sanity checks: 2 atoms, species O and O; geometry consistent with a diatomic O2 in the box\\n  - Bond length reported above is consistent with the SP geometry used for the final analysis.\\n\\nArtifacts referenced (project-files-relative paths)\\n- Final SP results and geometry:\\n  - vasp_runs/o2_sp/CONTCAR (SP run directory)\\n  - vasp_runs/o2_sp/CONTCAR/vasprun.xml (final energies)\\n  - vasp_runs/o2_sp/CONTCAR/CONTCAR (bond length/orientation; used for O–O distance)\\n  - vasp_runs/o2_sp/CONTCAR/OUTCAR (normal termination log)\\n- Summary for downstream use:\\n  - results/o2_vasp_summary.json\\n\\nNotes\\n- The SP inputs for this run were prepared in vasp_inputs/o2_sp/CONTCAR with triplet spin constraints enforced (ISPIN=2, NUPDOWN=2, MAGMOM=1 1). Final results reflect those settings.\\n\\nIf you’d like, I can export a compact JSON summary or compare these results to a reference benchmark for O2 in a similar box setup.\\n\"}","role":"user"}],"model":"openai/gpt-5-nano","stream":false,"temperature":1.0,"prompt_cache_retention":"24h"}
